 "text": "Auditor | Mills County, IA\nSkip To Main Content This website is AudioEye enabled and is being optimized for accessibility. To open the AudioEye Toolbar, press \"shift + =\". Some assistive technologies may require the use of a passthrough function before this keystroke. For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nEMERGENCY ALERT\n***Burn Ban Lifted***\nRead On...\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nHome\nGovernment\nServices\nOur Community\nHow Do I...\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment\nDepartments A - L\nAuditor\nAuditor\nThe County Auditor serves in an office that is very diversified.\nMain Functions\nThe main functions are:\nClerk to the Board of Supervisors\nCommissioner of Elections\nKeeping Real Estate Transfer Records\nMaintaining Financial Records\nPreparing and Certifying Tax Levies\nTax Rates & Budgets\nThe Auditor calculates tax rates for all taxing entities in the County by applying taxes levied by those entities to the valuation of each property and then prepares a tax list showing each taxpayer's share of the total. The Auditor also prepares the County's budget from material submitted by its departments and other agencies.\nHuman Resources\nThe Auditor is responsible for the preparation of payroll and management of the County's human resources. Claims against the county are reviewed in the Auditor's office and warrants in payment then are prepared. The Auditor's election responsibilities include registering voters, preparing all elections held within the county, supervising precinct election officials, publishing election notices, and acting as custodian of the poll books.\nElected Position\nThe County Auditor is an elected official with a term of four years.\nCigarette & Alcohol Licenses\nApplication for Iowa Retail Cigarette Permit (PDF)\nApplication for Iowa Alcohol License\nOther Forms\nFireworks Permit Application (PDF)\nIRS Form W-9 (PDF)\nQualification of Officer Not Required to Give Bond (PDF)\nSketch Plat Application (PDF)\nTownship Annual Report Instructions (PDF)\nState Fiscal Audit\nFY25 Audit Report PDF\nContact Us\nAmber Farnan\nAuditor\nMegan Major\nEmail about Real Estate questions\nAuditor\nEmail the Auditor\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n418 Sharp Street\nGlenwood , IA 51534\n418 Sharp Street Glenwood IA 51534\nDirections\nPhone: 712-527-3146\nFax: 712-527-1579\nHours\nMonday through Friday\n8 am to 4:30 pm\nDirectory\nElection Form Links\nVoter Election Forms\nCandidate Election Forms\nView All Election Form Links\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nVoting & Election\nAbsentee Voting\nElection Calendar\nElection Results Archive\nEthics & Campaign Disclosure\nMills County Elected Officials Current Terms\nUpcoming Elections\nPrimary Election\nGeneral Election\nCity/School Election\nSpecial Election\nVoting Law Changes - Identification Required\nWhere to Vote\nWho Can Register to Vote\nElection Open Records Requests\nPEO Portal\nNotary Services\nEmployee 1095-C Form\nBeacon Property Search\nAgendas & Minutes\nOnline Payments\nOrdinances & Resolutions\nEmployment Opportunities\nAlert Iowa Sign Up\n-->\nContact Us\n418 Sharp Street\nGlenwood, IA 51534\nContact Us\nQuick Links\nEmployee Login\nNotify Me\nAgendas & Minutes\nMillsAlert\nBoards and Commissions\nVoting and Elections\nPublic Information\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nHelpful Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\nPrivacy Policy\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by CivicPlus®\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nOpens in new window\nPDF Download\nWord Download\nExcel Download\nPowerPoint Download\nDocument Download\nExplore your accessibility options",
